,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A, all real y except y = a and y = -a","reason":"The numerator simplifies to (a^2+y^2)/(a^2-y^2), and the denominator is its negative. Since a ≠ 0, a^2+y^2 is positive. The value is therefore -1 exactly when y ≠ ±a.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1963_AMC_12_Q17","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_161","cnm_160","cnm_147"],"id":"common-denominator","label":"Simplify while preserving the domain","methodDirectNodeIds":{"common-denominator":["cnm_162","cnm_156"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_162","cnm_156","cnm_161","cnm_160","cnm_147"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, y^2","reason":"For |y|<1, the exact value is positive and the error is 1/(1+y)-(1-y)=y^2/(1+y). Dividing by 1/(1+y) gives y^2.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1965_AMC_12_Q18","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_027","cnm_147","cnm_160","cnm_161"],"id":"compute-relative-error","label":"Compute and divide the error","methodDirectNodeIds":{"compute-relative-error":["cnm_162"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_162","cnm_027","cnm_147","cnm_160","cnm_161"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"E, (m+n+2)/(mn-1)","reason":"For total rate T, A's and B's rates are T/(m+1) and T/(n+1). C's rate is T(mn-1)/[(m+1)(n+1)]. Therefore x=(rate A+rate B)/(rate C)=(m+n+2)/(mn-1).","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":["Positive individual work rates imply mn>1, ensuring the denominator is positive.","Positive work rates require m>0, n>0, and mn>1; in particular, the displayed denominator cannot vanish."],"questionId":"1965_AMC_12_Q38","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_p214","cnm_160","cnm_161"],"id":"solution:total-work-rate:9ae995439246","label":"Express each rate as part of the total","methodDirectNodeIds":{"total-work-rate":["cnm_046","cnm_162"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_046","cnm_162","cnm_p214","cnm_160","cnm_161"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"D, 2xy+2/(xy)","reason":"The common numerator is (x²+1)(y²+1)+(x²-1)(y²-1)=2x²y²+2. Dividing by xy gives 2xy+2/(xy), valid for xy≠0.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1967_AMC_12_Q02","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_160","cnm_161","cnm_156"],"id":"combine-over-common-denominator","label":"Combine over a common denominator","methodDirectNodeIds":{"combine-over-common-denominator":["cnm_162","cnm_146"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_162","cnm_146","cnm_160","cnm_161","cnm_156"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A. x(x+2)(x+5)/((x+1)(x+3)) days","reason":"The production rate per cow per day is (x+1)/(x(x+2)). With x+3 cows, producing x+5 cans therefore takes (x+5)/((x+3)(x+1)/(x(x+2)))=x(x+2)(x+5)/((x+1)(x+3)) days.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":["Assumes each cow produces milk at the same constant rate.","Assumes every cow produces milk at the same constant rate."],"questionId":"1976_AMC_12_Q13","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_160","cnm_p185"],"id":"proportional-scaling","label":"Scale the amount and the herd","methodDirectNodeIds":{"proportional-scaling":["cnm_p215","cnm_p213","cnm_p214"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_p215","cnm_p213","cnm_p214","cnm_160","cnm_p185"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":4,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"A (-1)","reason":"Let S=a+b+c. Adding 2 to the equal ratios gives S/a=S/b=S/c. If S≠0, then a=b=c and x=8, contrary to x<0. Thus S=0, so the three numerator factors are -c, -a, and -b, giving x=-1.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"ques